{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 1, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "phi(12) = 4\n  how: 12 = 2^2 * 3; phi = product of p^(e-1) (p - 1): 2^1*1 * 2\n  the order of the unit group (Z/12)*; lambda(12) = 2 is its exponent\n  check: counted the k in 1..12 with gcd(k, 12) = 1: 4\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 1, "ok": true, "cmd": "phi", "ucas": "phi 12", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "phi", "method": "12 = 2^2 * 3; phi = product of p^(e-1) (p - 1): 2^1*1 * 2", "lhs": "phi(12)", "value": "4", "value_int": 4, "headline": "phi(12) = 4", "details": ["the order of the unit group (Z/12)*; lambda(12) = 2 is its exponent"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "counted the k in 1..12 with gcd(k, 12) = 1: 4"}], "files": [], "text": "phi(12) = 4\n  how: 12 = 2^2 * 3; phi = product of p^(e-1) (p - 1): 2^1*1 * 2\n  the order of the unit group (Z/12)*; lambda(12) = 2 is its exponent\n  check: counted the k in 1..12 with gcd(k, 12) = 1: 4\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 2, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "lambda(561) = 80 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)\n  how: 561 = 3 * 11 * 17; lambda is the lcm of 2 (3^1), 10 (11^1), 16 (17^1)\n  lambda(2^e) = 2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(561) = 320\n  check: the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 80\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 2, "ok": true, "cmd": "carmichael", "ucas": "carmichael 561", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "carmichael", "method": "561 = 3 * 11 * 17; lambda is the lcm of 2 (3^1), 10 (11^1), 16 (17^1)", "lambda(2^e)": "2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(561) = 320", "headline": "lambda(561) = 80 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 80"}], "files": [], "text": "lambda(561) = 80 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)\n  how: 561 = 3 * 11 * 17; lambda is the lcm of 2 (3^1), 10 (11^1), 16 (17^1)\n  lambda(2^e) = 2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(561) = 320\n  check: the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 80\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 3, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "561 = 3 * 11 * 17 (not prime)\n  a Carmichael number: a^(n-1) = 1 for every a coprime to it (lambda(561) = 80 divides n - 1), so Fermat's test is fooled\n  how: trial division by the primes below 50, then Pollard-Brent rho; primality by Miller-Rabin with the first 12 prime bases (deterministic below 2^64)\n  check: the product is 561; each factor is prime\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 3, "ok": true, "cmd": "factorint", "ucas": "factorint 561", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "factorint", "a_carmichael_number": "a^(n-1) = 1 for every a coprime to it (lambda(561) = 80 divides n - 1), so Fermat's test is fooled", "method": "trial division by the primes below 50, then Pollard-Brent rho; primality by Miller-Rabin with the first 12 prime bases (deterministic below 2^64)", "lhs": "561", "annotation": "not prime", "value": "3 * 11 * 17", "headline": "561 = 3 * 11 * 17 (not prime)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the product is 561; each factor is prime"}], "files": [], "text": "561 = 3 * 11 * 17 (not prime)\n  a Carmichael number: a^(n-1) = 1 for every a coprime to it (lambda(561) = 80 divides n - 1), so Fermat's test is fooled\n  how: trial division by the primes below 50, then Pollard-Brent rho; primality by Miller-Rabin with the first 12 prime bases (deterministic below 2^64)\n  check: the product is 561; each factor is prime\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 4, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "(2/7) = 1\n  a quadratic residue: x^2 = a has a solution\n  (4^2 = 2 mod 7)\n  how: quadratic reciprocity (the binary Jacobi algorithm)\n  check: Euler's criterion 2^((7-1)/2) = 1 mod 7\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 4, "ok": true, "cmd": "legendre", "ucas": "legendre 2 7", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "legendre", "a_quadratic_residue": "x^2 = a has a solution", "method": "quadratic reciprocity (the binary Jacobi algorithm)", "lhs": "(2/7)", "value": "1", "value_int": 1, "headline": "(2/7) = 1", "details": ["(4^2 = 2 mod 7)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "Euler's criterion 2^((7-1)/2) = 1 mod 7"}], "files": [], "text": "(2/7) = 1\n  a quadratic residue: x^2 = a has a solution\n  (4^2 = 2 mod 7)\n  how: quadratic reciprocity (the binary Jacobi algorithm)\n  check: Euler's criterion 2^((7-1)/2) = 1 mod 7\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 5, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "(2/15) = 1\n  how: quadratic reciprocity; the product of the Legendre symbols over 15 = 3 * 5\n  15 is composite: (a/n) = 1 does not make a a square mod n; here 2 is not a square mod 15\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 5, "ok": true, "cmd": "jacobi", "ucas": "jacobi 2 15", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "jacobi", "method": "quadratic reciprocity; the product of the Legendre symbols over 15 = 3 * 5", "15_is_composite": "(a/n) = 1 does not make a a square mod n; here 2 is not a square mod 15", "lhs": "(2/15)", "value": "1", "value_int": 1, "headline": "(2/15) = 1"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "(2/15) = 1\n  how: quadratic reciprocity; the product of the Legendre symbols over 15 = 3 * 5\n  15 is composite: (a/n) = 1 does not make a a square mod n; here 2 is not a square mod 15\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 6, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x^2 = 2 mod 7: x = 3, 4\n  how: p = 3 mod 4: x = a^((p+1)/4)\n  check: 3^2 = 2, 4^2 = 2 (mod 7); brute force over 0..6: 2 solutions\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 6, "ok": true, "cmd": "sqrtmod", "ucas": "sqrtmod 2 mod 7", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "sqrtmod", "modulus": "7", "solutions": 2, "roots": [3, 4], "method": "p = 3 mod 4: x = a^((p+1)/4)", "headline": "x^2 = 2 mod 7: x = 3, 4"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "3^2 = 2, 4^2 = 2 (mod 7); brute force over 0..6: 2 solutions"}], "files": [], "text": "x^2 = 2 mod 7: x = 3, 4\n  how: p = 3 mod 4: x = a^((p+1)/4)\n  check: 3^2 = 2, 4^2 = 2 (mod 7); brute force over 0..6: 2 solutions\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 7, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x^2 = 1 mod 15: x = 1, 4, 11, 14\n  how: 15 = 3 * 5: roots mod each prime (Tonelli-Shanks), lifted to the prime powers (Hensel), combined by CRT\n  check: 1^2 = 1, 4^2 = 1, 11^2 = 1, 14^2 = 1 (mod 15); brute force over 0..14: 4 solutions\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 7, "ok": true, "cmd": "sqrtmod", "ucas": "sqrtmod 1 mod 15", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "sqrtmod", "modulus": "15", "solutions": 4, "roots": [1, 4, 11, 14], "method": "15 = 3 * 5: roots mod each prime (Tonelli-Shanks), lifted to the prime powers (Hensel), combined by CRT", "headline": "x^2 = 1 mod 15: x = 1, 4, 11, 14"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "1^2 = 1, 4^2 = 1, 11^2 = 1, 14^2 = 1 (mod 15); brute force over 0..14: 4 solutions"}], "files": [], "text": "x^2 = 1 mod 15: x = 1, 4, 11, 14\n  how: 15 = 3 * 5: roots mod each prime (Tonelli-Shanks), lifted to the prime powers (Hensel), combined by CRT\n  check: 1^2 = 1, 4^2 = 1, 11^2 = 1, 14^2 = 1 (mod 15); brute force over 0..14: 4 solutions\n"}, "isError": false}}
