{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 9, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the squares mod 7: 4 of 7 residues\n  0, 1, 2, 4\n  7 is prime: the nonzero squares are (p-1)/2 = 3, the a with (a/p) = 1\n  how: x^2 mod 7 for every x\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 9, "ok": true, "cmd": "qr", "ucas": "qr 7", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "qr", "7_is_prime": "the nonzero squares are (p-1)/2 = 3, the a with (a/p) = 1", "method": "x^2 mod 7 for every x", "headline": "the squares mod 7: 4 of 7 residues", "details": ["0, 1, 2, 4"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "the squares mod 7: 4 of 7 residues\n  0, 1, 2, 4\n  7 is prime: the nonzero squares are (p-1)/2 = 3, the a with (a/p) = 1\n  how: x^2 mod 7 for every x\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 10, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the smallest primitive root mod 7 is 3\n  how: (Z/7)* is cyclic of order phi = 6 = 2 * 3; g generates it iff g^(6/p) != 1 for each prime p | 6\n  phi(6) = 2 primitive roots: 3 5\n  check: the powers 3^0 .. 3^5 are 6 distinct units\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 10, "ok": true, "cmd": "primroot", "ucas": "primroot 7", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "primroot", "value": "3", "method": "(Z/7)* is cyclic of order phi = 6 = 2 * 3; g generates it iff g^(6/p) != 1 for each prime p | 6", "phi(6)": "2 primitive roots: 3 5", "headline": "the smallest primitive root mod 7 is 3"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the powers 3^0 .. 3^5 are 6 distinct units"}], "files": [], "text": "the smallest primitive root mod 7 is 3\n  how: (Z/7)* is cyclic of order phi = 6 = 2 * 3; g generates it iff g^(6/p) != 1 for each prime p | 6\n  phi(6) = 2 primitive roots: 3 5\n  check: the powers 3^0 .. 3^5 are 6 distinct units\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 11, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "yes: 3 is a primitive root mod 7 (its order is 6, phi(7) = 6)\n  how: 3^(6/2) = 6, 3^(6/3) = 2 (a primitive root has none of these equal to 1)\n  check: the powers 3^0 .. 3^5 are 6 distinct units\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 11, "ok": true, "cmd": "primroot", "ucas": "primroot 3 mod 7", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "primroot", "primitive_root": true, "order": "6", "phi": "6", "method": "3^(6/2) = 6, 3^(6/3) = 2 (a primitive root has none of these equal to 1)", "headline": "yes: 3 is a primitive root mod 7 (its order is 6, phi(7) = 6)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the powers 3^0 .. 3^5 are 6 distinct units"}], "files": [], "text": "yes: 3 is a primitive root mod 7 (its order is 6, phi(7) = 6)\n  how: 3^(6/2) = 6, 3^(6/3) = 2 (a primitive root has none of these equal to 1)\n  check: the powers 3^0 .. 3^5 are 6 distinct units\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 12, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "3^-1 = 4 mod 11\n  how: extended Euclid: 4*3 - 1*11 = 1\n  check: 3 * 4 = 12 = 1*11 + 1\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 12, "ok": true, "cmd": "inverse_mod", "ucas": "inverse 3 mod 11", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "inverse", "method": "extended Euclid: 4*3 - 1*11 = 1", "lhs": "3^-1", "modulus": "11", "value": "4", "value_int": 4, "headline": "3^-1 = 4 mod 11"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "3 * 4 = 12 = 1*11 + 1"}], "files": [], "text": "3^-1 = 4 mod 11\n  how: extended Euclid: 4*3 - 1*11 = 1\n  check: 3 * 4 = 12 = 1*11 + 1\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 13, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "ord(3) = 6 mod 7\n  how: the order divides lambda(7) = 6; 3^6 = 1 and 3^(6/2) = 6, 3^(6/3) = 2\n  3 is a primitive root mod 7 (its order is phi(7) = 6)\n  additive order: 7\n  check: stepping through the powers, 3^k = 1 first at k = 6\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 13, "ok": true, "cmd": "order_mod", "ucas": "order 3 mod 7", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "order", "method": "the order divides lambda(7) = 6; 3^6 = 1 and 3^(6/2) = 6, 3^(6/3) = 2", "additive_order": "7", "lhs": "ord(3)", "modulus": "7", "value": "6", "value_int": 6, "headline": "ord(3) = 6 mod 7", "details": ["3 is a primitive root mod 7 (its order is phi(7) = 6)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "stepping through the powers, 3^k = 1 first at k = 6"}], "files": [], "text": "ord(3) = 6 mod 7\n  how: the order divides lambda(7) = 6; 3^6 = 1 and 3^(6/2) = 6, 3^(6/3) = 2\n  3 is a primitive root mod 7 (its order is phi(7) = 6)\n  additive order: 7\n  check: stepping through the powers, 3^k = 1 first at k = 6\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 14, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the system\n  x = 2 mod 3: x = 2\n    x = 2 (mod 3)\n  x = 3 mod 5: x = 3\n    x = 3 (mod 5)\nx = 8 (mod 15)\n  how: the Chinese remainder theorem, pairwise (moduli that share factors must agree mod their gcd)\n  check: the solution substituted into every congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..14: 1 solution\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 14, "ok": true, "cmd": "crt", "ucas": "crt x = 2 mod 3, x = 3 mod 5", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "crt", "solutions": ["8"], "modulus": "15", "x": ["2 mod 3: x = 2", "2 (mod 3)", "3 mod 5: x = 3", "3 (mod 5)"], "method": "the Chinese remainder theorem, pairwise (moduli that share factors must agree mod their gcd)", "headline": "the system", "more": ["x = 8 (mod 15)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the solution substituted into every congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..14: 1 solution"}], "files": [], "text": "the system\n  x = 2 mod 3: x = 2\n    x = 2 (mod 3)\n  x = 3 mod 5: x = 3\n    x = 3 (mod 5)\nx = 8 (mod 15)\n  how: the Chinese remainder theorem, pairwise (moduli that share factors must agree mod their gcd)\n  check: the solution substituted into every congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..14: 1 solution\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 15, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  3 * x = 1 mod 11: 3x = 1: x = 1 * 3^-1 = 1 * 4 = 4\nx = 4 (mod 11)\n  check: the solution substituted into the congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..10: 1 solution\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 15, "ok": true, "cmd": "congruence", "ucas": "congruence 3*x = 1 mod 11", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "congruence", "solutions": ["4"], "modulus": "11", "lhs": "x", "annotation": "mod 11", "value": "4", "value_int": 4, "headline": "x = 4 (mod 11)", "details": ["3 * x = 1 mod 11: 3x = 1: x = 1 * 3^-1 = 1 * 4 = 4"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the solution substituted into the congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..10: 1 solution"}], "files": [], "text": "  3 * x = 1 mod 11: 3x = 1: x = 1 * 3^-1 = 1 * 4 = 4\nx = 4 (mod 11)\n  check: the solution substituted into the congruence: it holds; brute force over 0..10: 1 solution\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 16, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "x / 7 for unsigned x: u32\n  m = ceil(2^35 / 7) = 4908534053 (0x124924925, 33 bits), shift s = 3\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^35)\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*7 = 2^35 + e with e = 3 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^35 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^35), and x*e/2^35 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer\n  m has 33 bits, one more than u32: the usual sequence uses m - 2^32 = 0x24924925 and an add that cannot overflow:\n    C:    t = mulhi(x, 0x24924925); q = (t + ((x - t) >> 1)) >> 2;\n    in ucas: (u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32) + ((x - u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32)) >> 1)) >> 2\n  check: the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 7 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 7 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 16, "ok": true, "cmd": "magic", "ucas": "magic 7 u32", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "magic", "m": "ceil(2^35 / 7) = 4908534053 (0x124924925, 33 bits), shift s = 3", "q": "floor(x * m / 2^35)", "proof_granlund_montgomery": "m*7 = 2^35 + e with e = 3 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^35 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^35), and x*e/2^35 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer", "m_has_33_bits_one_more_than_u32": "the usual sequence uses m - 2^32 = 0x24924925 and an add that cannot overflow:", "c": "   t = mulhi(x, 0x24924925); q = (t + ((x - t) >> 1)) >> 2;", "in_ucas": "(u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32) + ((x - u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32)) >> 1)) >> 2", "headline": "x / 7 for unsigned x: u32"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 7 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)"}, {"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 7 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)"}], "files": [], "text": "x / 7 for unsigned x: u32\n  m = ceil(2^35 / 7) = 4908534053 (0x124924925, 33 bits), shift s = 3\n  q = floor(x * m / 2^35)\n  proof (Granlund-Montgomery): m*7 = 2^35 + e with e = 3 <= 2^3.  Write x = q*7 + r, 0 <= r < 7.  Then x*m/2^35 = x/7 + x*e/(7*2^35), and x*e/2^35 < 1 because |x| < 2^32, so the extra term is below 1/7: it cannot carry r/7 <= 6/7 past the next integer\n  m has 33 bits, one more than u32: the usual sequence uses m - 2^32 = 0x24924925 and an add that cannot overflow:\n    C:    t = mulhi(x, 0x24924925); q = (t + ((x - t) >> 1)) >> 2;\n    in ucas: (u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32) + ((x - u32((u64(x) * 0x24924925) >> 32)) >> 1)) >> 2\n  check: the ucas form above, run by ucas's evaluator in u32, equals x / 7 for the 256 smallest and largest x and 65536 random x (66048 inputs)\n  check: the sequence above, emulated in 32-bit arithmetic, equals x / 7 (C's truncating division) for the ends of the range, both sides of the multiples of d near 0 and near the top, and 2^20 random inputs (1073152 inputs)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 17, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "2^x = 4 in Z/7: x = 2 (mod 3, the order of 2)\n  how: Pohlig-Hellman over 3 = 3, baby-step giant-step for each prime\n  check: 2^2 = 4\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 17, "ok": true, "cmd": "dlog", "ucas": "dlog 4 base 2 mod 7", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "dlog", "value": "2", "modulus": "3", "base": "2", "method": "Pohlig-Hellman over 3 = 3, baby-step giant-step for each prime", "headline": "2^x = 4 in Z/7: x = 2 (mod 3, the order of 2)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "2^2 = 4"}], "files": [], "text": "2^x = 4 in Z/7: x = 2 (mod 3, the order of 2)\n  how: Pohlig-Hellman over 3 = 3, baby-step giant-step for each prime\n  check: 2^2 = 4\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 18, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  units: phi(12) = 4: 1, 5, 7, 11\n  unit group: C2 x C2 (order 4, exponent lambda(12) = 2); not cyclic, so there is no primitive root\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 18, "ok": true, "cmd": "ring", "ucas": "ring Z/12 units", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "ring", "units": "phi(12) = 4: 1, 5, 7, 11", "unit_group": "C2 x C2 (order 4, exponent lambda(12) = 2); not cyclic, so there is no primitive root"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "  units: phi(12) = 4: 1, 5, 7, 11\n  unit group: C2 x C2 (order 4, exponent lambda(12) = 2); not cyclic, so there is no primitive root\n"}, "isError": false}}
